{
  "_comment": [
    "The shared truth table for account classification. The engine",
    "(crates/ledgeline-core/src/reports/account_types.rs) and the browser",
    "(web/src/lib/domain/accountTypes.ts) are two implementations of one",
    "specification, and BOTH are checked against this file:",
    "  - crates/ledgeline-core/tests/account_types.rs",
    "  - web/src/lib/domain/accountTypes.test.ts",
    "",
    "They must agree, and 'read the same journal differently' is not a cosmetic",
    "defect. An account the browser cannot type falls all the way through to",
    "ENGLISH NAME INFERENCE, so `income:contractors ; type: expenses` resolved as",
    "revenue in the browser and as expense in the engine makes the Projections",
    "tab negate a cost — and an expense that pays money IN builds cash forever",
    "(plan 22, amendment 42).",
    "",
    "`type` is the resolved type (null = untyped). `isRevenue`/`isExpense`/",
    "`isAsset`/`isEquity` are the SUBTYPE-FOLDING membership tests, which are",
    "what every classification should call: cash is an asset, gain is a revenue,",
    "conversion is an equity.",
    "",
    "Add a row here rather than a one-sided unit test. A test in only one language",
    "cannot catch the two drifting, which is the entire failure mode."
  ],
